    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and both tests pass with a green build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional owner registration dates for `POST /api/owners`, defaulting to the server's current date when omitted and returning the value in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is an `allOf` over `OwnerFields`, this makes the field bindable on the create body and returned on the owner response, generating a `LocalDate` field on both `OwnerFieldsDto` and `OwnerDto`. MapStruct maps it automatically in both directions (no mapper change needed).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field with `@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`, plus its getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. hsqldb is the one exercised by tests; the others are kept consistent.\n\n4. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** (new) \u2014 A small single-responsibility pipeline step: if the built owner has no registration date, it sets `LocalDate.now()` in place; a supplied date is left untouched.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new `defaultRegistrationDate` step between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe defaulting logic lives in its own step rather than being folded into `BuildOwner` (which stays focused on constructing the entity from the body), matching the project's function-injection conventions. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, satisfying both the \"defaults to today\" and \"keeps supplied date\" acceptance tests.",
